The Methodist Church in Bodie State Historic Park was built in **1882**.

It's the only church still standing in the ghost town — a Catholic church also went up in Bodie the same year, but it was destroyed in a 1928 fire, as [Flying Dawn Marie](w1) notes in her self-guided tour write-up. The same 1882 date is given by [Amateur Traveler](w2), which calls it Bodie's first church. It sits on Fuller Street near the start of the walk into town, and visitors today can still peer in at the organ, pulpit and benches inside the slowly decaying building, per [losethemap](w3).

