The attraction you're after is **Illumination's Villain-Con Minion Blast**, in Minion Land on Illumination Avenue at Universal Studios Florida. It's exactly the "not a sit-down ride" format you described: you stand on a moving walkway (an omni-mover) and hold a blaster, shooting at villains projected on screens all around you as you glide through the scenes. According to [Wishes Family Travel](w2), it's an "interactive attraction" rather than a traditional ride — a game you play while moving through a convention-themed queue full of vendor booths and gag "speaker" listings. [Bridges and Balloons](w3) called it their kids' favourite attraction at the park, noting you can link your blaster to the Universal app to log scores and compete against your own previous runs; they add that kids roughly 3 and up can manage the blaster, though it is a shooting game if that's a concern. The line tends to move quickly since the conveyor handles many players at once.

It sits right beside the older **Despicable Me Minion Mayhem** (a motion-simulator ride, so more traditional) and the **Illumination's Minion Cafe** if you want to pair it with a meal.

